    "waarom": "Valuable and complex products such as electronics, batteries, photovoltaic (PV) panels, and other specialized products require dedicated collection, sorting and processing infrastructure. Conventional municipal collection systems may not capture these product streams at sufficient scale or quality. Products may be dispersed across households, businesses and public organizations, while some streams contain hazardous substances or require specific handling and transport conditions. As a result, valuable materials can be lost, causing environmental and safety risks and moreover, opportunities for regional recovery and recycling can remain untapped. Municipalities and regions need better insight into where valuable waste streams arise, how they can be collected and processed most effectively, which recycling routes are economically viable, and how future waste streams and material recovery opportunities are expected to evolve over time.",
