    "id": "circulariteit-lifetime-extension-nl-verlengen",
    "domain": "circulariteit",
    "name": "Lifetime Extension (NL: Verlengen)",
    "intro": "Lifetime extension focuses on keeping products, components and materials in use for as long as possible through reuse, repair, refurbishment, remanufacturing and repurposing. By extending product lifetimes, municipalities can reduce waste generation, lower the environmental impact of consumption, and retain the value embedded in products for longer. These strategies can also contribute to resource security by reducing dependence on imported materials, particularly Critical Raw Materials (CRMs), which are increasingly subject to geopolitical developments and supply chain risks. At the same time, repair, refurbishment and remanufacturing activities can strengthen local economies by creating business opportunities, skilled jobs and opportunities for social enterprises and SMEs. Realizing these benefits requires not only technical solutions, but also insight into where the largest opportunities exist, an understanding of behavioral barriers, the availability of repair skills and infrastructure, and mechanisms that connect supply and demand for reusable products. The following use cases illustrate how municipalities can use data, analysis, digital technologies, education and policy instruments to stimulate product lifetime extension, strengthen local circular value chains, and increase resilience to future material supply challenges.\nThis use case consists of five sub-use cases:\nIdentifying priority products and materials\nUnderstanding behavioural barriers and motivators\nStrengthening repair skills and support networks\nConnecting supply and demand for circular use\nLeveraging public procurement for circular products",
